  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **China Cat Sunflower** (1 other source): China Cat Sunflower flows straight into I Know You Rider [3]\n- **He's Gone** (1 other source): He's Gone leads into Smokestack Lightnin', then returns to He's Gone before moving into Let it Grow [3]\n- **Dark Star** (1 other source): Dark Star follows Drums and Space, and Morning Dew comes after it [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Smokestack Lightnin'**: rare: 14 archived performances [10]\n- **Space jam**: rare: 4 archived performances [10]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Next Time You See Me [10]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadandco2016-07-03.akg481** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 174 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording has the sound of standing right in front of the stage [4]\n- **DeadandCompany2016-07-03.hiandlo**: audience recording; 17 songs; 172 min [2]\n- **deadco2016-07-03**: source not stated; 18 songs; 171 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer feels this is the best of the shows they have followed on this tour, though variety makes picking hard [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadandco2016-07-03.akg481**: taped by Jeff Frank; transferred by Jeff Frank; source: AKG 481 > V3 > Marantz PMD661 (16/44.1) fob [1]\n- **DeadandCompany2016-07-03.hiandlo**: taped by hi and lo; transferred by nyctaper; source: AUD [2]\n- **deadco2016-07-03**: taped by paulr; transferred by paulr; source: EarthworksSR77>Grace V3>TascamHDP2 [3]",
   "citations": [
